---
.title = "Read arguments as a slice",
.date = "2026-09-02",
.author = "muhammadSwa",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Collect every command line argument at once with [`std.process.Args.toSlice`]. Like the other recipes in this chapter, this uses the Zig 0.16 [`std.process.Init`] entry point (`pub fn main(init: std.process.Init)`) and `init.minimal.args`. `toSlice` requires an arena allocator (`init.arena.allocator()`); the arena reclaims the memory at process exit, so no manual `free` is needed.

Reach for this when you need random access to the arguments or want to store them.

[]($code.siteAsset('src/13-02.zig').language('zig'))

